{"a1":[{"k":"title","cap":"Overlaps of Two Schedules","say":"Let's solve Overlaps of Two Schedules, using the Two Pointers approach.","card":{"title":"Overlaps of Two Schedules","sub":"Two Pointers · Medium","pattern":"two-pointers"}},{"k":"problem","cap":"a and b are lists of closed intervals, each list sorted and non-overlapping. Return the intersection of the two schedules: every overlap [max start, min end] between an interval of a and an interval of b.","say":"a and b are lists of closed intervals, each list sorted and non-overlapping. Return the intersection of the two schedules: every overlap max start, min end between an interval of a and an interval of b.","card":{"lines":["a and b are lists of closed intervals, each list sorted and non-overlapping. Return the intersection of the two schedules: every overlap [max start, min end] between an interval of a and an interval of b."]}},{"k":"example","cap":"For example, with a = [[0,2],[5,10],[13,23],[24,25]], b = [[1,5],[8,12],[15,24],[25,26]], the answer is [[1,2],[5,5],[8,10],[15,23],[24,24],[25,25]].","say":"For example, with a equals 0, 2, 5, 10, 13, 23, 24, 25, b equals 1, 5, 8, 12, 15, 24, 25, 26, the answer is 1, 2, 5, 5, 8, 10, 15, 23, 24, 24, 25, 25.","card":{"lines":["Input: a = [[0,2],[5,10],[13,23],[24,25]], b = [[1,5],[8,12],[15,24],[25,26]]","Output: [[1,2],[5,5],[8,10],[15,23],[24,24],[25,25]]"]}},{"k":"idea","cap":"Point I at an interval in a and J at one in b. Their overlap, if any, runs from the later start to the earlier end.","card":{"pattern":"two-pointers","name":"Two Pointers"}},{"k":"idea","cap":"Then advance the pointer whose interval ends first, because it can't overlap anything later in the other list.","card":{"pattern":"two-pointers","name":"Two Pointers"}},{"k":"trace","cap":"Let's walk through it with a = [[0,2],[5,10],[13,23],[24,25]], b = [[1,5],[8,12],[15,24],[25,26]].","say":"Let's walk through it with a equals 0, 2, 5, 10, 13, 23, 24, 25, b equals 1, 5, 8, 12, 15, 24, 25, 26.","st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"0"},{"k":"j","v":"0"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0]]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"[0, 2] and [1, 5] overlap on [1, 2].","say":"0, 2 and 1, 5 overlap on 1, 2.","ln":{"python":6,"java":6},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"0"},{"k":"j","v":"0"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0]]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"[5, 10] and [1, 5] overlap on [5, 5].","say":"5, 10 and 1, 5 overlap on 5, 5.","ln":{"python":6,"java":6},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"1"},{"k":"j","v":"0"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0],[5.0,5.0]]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"[5, 10] and [8, 12] overlap on [8, 10].","say":"5, 10 and 8, 12 overlap on 8, 10.","ln":{"python":6,"java":6},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"1"},{"k":"j","v":"1"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0],[5.0,5.0],[8.0,10.0]]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"[13, 23] and [15, 24] overlap on [15, 23].","say":"13, 23 and 15, 24 overlap on 15, 23.","ln":{"python":6,"java":6},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"2"},{"k":"j","v":"2"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0],[5.0,5.0],[8.0,10.0],[15.0,23.0]]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"[24, 25] and [15, 24] overlap on [24, 24].","say":"24, 25 and 15, 24 overlap on 24, 24.","ln":{"python":6,"java":6},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"3"},{"k":"j","v":"2"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0],[5.0,5.0],[8.0,10.0],[15.0,23.0],[24.0,24.0]]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"[24, 25] and [25, 26] overlap on [25, 25].","say":"24, 25 and 25, 26 overlap on 25, 25.","ln":{"python":6,"java":6},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"3"},{"k":"j","v":"3"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0],[5.0,5.0],[8.0,10.0],[15.0,23.0],[24.0,24.0],[25.0,25.0]]}]}},{"k":"done","cap":"The answer is [[1,2],[5,5],[8,10],[15,23],[24,24],[25,25]].","say":"The answer is 1, 2, 5, 5, 8, 10, 15, 23, 24, 24, 25, 25.","st":{"vars":[{"k":"i","v":"3"},{"k":"j","v":"3"}],"intervals":[{"n":"a","v":[[0.0,2.0],[5.0,10.0],[13.0,23.0],[24.0,25.0]]},{"n":"b","v":[[1.0,5.0],[8.0,12.0],[15.0,24.0],[25.0,26.0]]},{"n":"overlaps","v":[[1.0,2.0],[5.0,5.0],[8.0,10.0],[15.0,23.0],[24.0,24.0],[25.0,25.0]]}]}},{"k":"complexity","cap":"Time complexity is O(n + m) and extra space is O(1) extra.","say":"Time complexity is O of n plus m and extra space is O of one extra.","card":{"time":"O(n + m)","space":"O(1) extra"}},{"k":"outro","cap":"That's the Two Pointers approach. Now try writing it yourself, in Java or Python!"}]}